# Mechanism: wgpu-animation

command: python3 -B scripts/check-wgpu-animation.py
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms/wgpu-animation
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - build.rs
  - src
  - crates
  - reactive-tui-macros
  - examples
  - tests
  - scripts
requirements:
  - GPU-003

The validator must reject frame-count rotation, an accumulating pending queue,
and an absent deadline gate using safe source fixtures. Corrected fixtures pass.
The Rust tests exercise the production clock and worker with a deterministic
elapsed-time schedule, a deliberately blocked first frame, many replacement
requests, shutdown, and invalid dimensions. They require at most one active
and one pending request, and no frame before its deadline.
A hardware smoke check renders distinct elapsed-time frames without input.
